Hi,
I'm trying to execute some commands from Biobase with JRI Rengine.
This is my code:

     String[] args2=new String[1];
     args2[0]="--save";

        re=new Rengine(args2, false, null);
        REXP x=re.eval("matrix(1:9,3,3)");
        int a[]=x.asIntArray();
        for(int i=0;i<a.length;i++)
            {
            System.out.println(a[i]);
            }
        re.eval("library(Biobase)");

        x=re.eval("Adata=read.exprSet(\"C:\\dataSample_1.txt\")");
        if(x==null)    System.out.println("Error!");

Well, it works fine with usual orders as matrix or so, and it even loads 
correctly "library(Biobase)", but then it seems to crash when evaluating 
read.exprSet.
Any ideas?

Thanks very much in advance!!

